    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87), who stands as our premier play today against Bailey Ober. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from both a favorable park factor and a slow-delivering opposing starter, which creates a prime environment for him to exploit the stolen base category, our highest priority. **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.86) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) also offer elite upside; **Luis Robert Jr.** carries a significant platoon advantage against the lefty Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned well in the order to drive in runs against Patrick Sandoval. We are also expecting strong production from **Kyle Tucker** (71.17), whose steady base projection remains bolstered by his favorable matchup against the right-handed Michael Wacha.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal range, specifically the benching of **Nasim Nunez** (47.78). While **Nasim Nunez** is a high-upside speed threat, the optimizer favored the structural stability of **Sam Antonacci** and **Coby Mayo** in the starting nine, despite the latter's platoon risk. **Jackson Merrill** (39.02) was also considered, but his poor matchup against the elite-arm efficiency of Kyle Harrison (2.92 xERA) made him an easy exclusion for today\u2019s card. Owners should monitor official lineups closely, as many of these scores are tethered to assumed batting order positions; should **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson** shift significantly down the order, we may see their efficiency scores dip below the 50-point threshold. Overall, the lineup is well-constructed to chase speed and counting stats, provided the weather holds and our core stars avoid late-scratch complications.",
